            "result_text": "The regex has been saved to `/app/regex.txt`. \n\nHere's how it works:\n\n1. **`^(?=.*IPv4_pattern)` (lookahead):** Checks that the line contains an IPv4 address with word boundaries (not preceded/followed by alphanumeric characters)\n\n2. **`.*?` (non-greedy):** Matches characters up to a date, finding the rightmost match due to the negative lookahead\n\n3. **`(?<![A-Za-z0-9])(date_capture)(?![A-Za-z0-9])`:** Captures the date with word boundary enforcement\n\n4. **`(?!.*date_pattern)` (negative lookahead):** Ensures no additional dates follow this one on the line\n\n5. **`.*$`:** Matches to the end of the line\n\nThe pattern correctly:\n- Rejects dates like \"1134-12-1234\" (invalid month/day) and \"2024-02-30\" (invalid day for February)\n- Requires valid dates: Jan-Dec have proper day ranges, Feb accepts 01-29\n- Enforces word boundaries to avoid matching embedded numbers like in \"user1134-12-12user\"\n- Returns only the last date in lines with multiple dates"
        }
